<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uttaradit</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uttaradit is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> on the Nan river and the capital of Uttaradit Province. The area was an important river port linking northern Thailand with the central plains. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1767 the nearby town of Sawangkhaburi was the base of the monk-ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chao-phra-fang">Chao Phra Fang</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">King Taksin</a> subdued him in 1770.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uttaradit.jpg" alt="Uttaradit" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ผู้สร้างสรรค์ผลงาน/ส่งข้อมูลเก็บในคลังข้อมูลเสรีวิกิมีเดียคอมมอนส์ - เทวประภาส มากคล้าย · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nan_river_in_Uttaradit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
